  chef: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 556ecd75ee852ce4a93c60357c4eb4f6, type: 2}
  letterBody: 'Ciao again!


    Your carbonara is getting good reviews. Brava! Now
    we go further.


    Margherita was named after a queen, but I learned it from
    a very loud baker in Naples who shouted at me every day for a whole summer. On
    my last day he gave me his dough knife and said I was "not hopeless." The highest
    praise of my life.


    Flour, water, yeast, and time. Stretch by hand, never
    a rolling pin. Tomato, mozzarella, fresh basil, a very hot oven.


    Sometimes
    the people who push you hardest believe in you the most.'
